\p
\v 4 \add ≈So¦100366\add* Yehoshua¦100367 called¦100366 \add over\add* the twelve men, one from¦100383 each tribe¦100383,
\v 5 and¦100385 told¦100385 them¦100386, “Cross¦100388 \add ≈back to¦100389 where\add* your¦100392 god¦100392 Yahweh's¦100391 box¦100390 is in¦100393 the¦100395 middle¦100395 of¦100395 the¦100396 Yordan¦100396 and¦100397 \add ≈each of you should pick¦100397 up¦100397 a¦100400 rock¦100400 and carry it back on your\add* shoulder—one¦100401 stone¦100400 each on¦100402 your shoulder¦100404 to¦100405 match the¦100405 number¦100405 of¦100405 tribes¦100406 of¦100406 Yisra'el's¦100409 sons.
\v 6 \add ≈Those boulders will¦100418 be¦100412 a¦100414 monument for all the people\add*. \add ≈In¦100415 the future when your¦100415 children¦100419 ask¦100421 what¦100422 those boulders mean\add*,
\v 7 then¦100427 you'll¦100427 all be able to¦100428 tell¦100427 them¦100428 that¦100429 the¦100431 water¦100431 in the¦100432 Yordan¦100432 \add River\add* was¦100430 cut¦100430 off¦100430 ahead of¦100433 the¦100434 box¦100434 with Yahweh's¦100437 agreement¦100435. When¦100438 it¦100438 crossed¦100438 over into¦100439 the river, the water¦100441 in the¦100442 river \add ≈stopped flowing\add*, and¦100443 those¦100445 boulders¦100444 are¦100443 a¦100446 memorial¦100446 for¦100447 the¦100447 Israelis¦100448 forever¦100451.
\p
\v 8 \add ≈So¦100455\add* the¦100456 Israelis¦100458 did just¦100460 what Yehoshua¦100462 had¦100461 told¦100461 them to do, and¦100463 they¦100463 picked¦100463 up¦100463 twelve boulders¦100467 from¦100468 the Yordan¦100469, just¦100470 as¦100470 Yahweh¦100472 had¦100471 instructed Yehoshua¦100475, and¦100481 brought¦100481 them¦100481 over¦100481 to¦100483 where \add the people\add* were camping and¦100486 placed¦100486 them¦100486 down¦100486 there¦100487.
\v 9 Then¦100489 Yehoshua¦100493 stacked up¦100492 twelve other boulders¦100491 in¦100494 the¦100494 middle¦100494 of¦100495 the¦100495 Yordan¦100495 where the¦100498 feet¦100498 of¦100498 the¦100499 priests¦100499 carrying¦100500 the¦100501 box¦100501 with the¦100502 agreement¦100502 had been¦100503, and¦100503 they¦100503 remain there¦100504 until¦100505 today.
\v 10 The¦100509 priests¦100509 carrying¦100510 the¦100511 box¦100511 had stood¦100512 in¦100513 the¦100513 middle¦100513 of¦100514 the¦100514 Yordan¦100514 until¦100515 everything¦100517 that¦100520 Yahweh¦100523 had¦100522 instructed¦100522 Yehoshua¦100526 to¦100527 pass¦100541 on to¦100528 the¦100530 people¦100530 was done, just as Mosheh¦100535 had¦100534 \add also\add* instructed¦100534 Yehoshua¦100538, and¦100539 the¦100540 people¦100540 had rapidly crossed¦100541 over¦100541.
\p
\v 11 As soon as all¦100547 the¦100549 people¦100549 had¦100546 crossed¦100550 over¦100550, the¦100552 priests¦100555 carrying Yahweh's¦100554 box¦100552 \add also\add* crossed¦100551 over in¦100556 front¦100556 of¦100556 the¦100557 people¦100557.
\v 12 The¦100560 \add soldiers\add* from the¦100567 tribes¦100567 of Reuben¦100562, and¦100563 Gad¦100565 and¦100566 the¦100566 half-tribe of¦100566 Menashsheh¦100568 had \add ≈marched\add* over¦100559 ahead of the rest of the Israeli¦100572, as¦100573 Mosheh¦100576 had¦100574 \add ≈agreed with them¦100575\add*.
\v 13 (\add There were\add* around¦100578 forty¦100578 thousand¦100579 of them, armed and ready for¦100585 battle¦100585, and they were heading to¦100586 the¦100587 plains¦100587 of¦100587 Yeriho¦100588 \add !(Jericho¦100588)\add* for the battle \add there\add*.)
\v 14 On that¦100592 day¦100591, Yahweh¦100594 helped Yehoshua¦100597 to look powerful¦100593 in¦100598 the eyes¦100598 of¦100598 the people, and¦100602 they¦100602 respected him¦100603 just¦100604 as¦100604 they¦100605 had¦100605 respected¦100605 Mosheh¦100608 all¦100609 the¦100611 days¦100611 of¦100611 his¦100612\f + \fr 4:14 \ft The Hebrew doesn't make it clear here whether the writer meant all of \+bd Mosheh's life\+bd* or all of \+bd Yehoshua's life\+bd*, so translations will vary.\f* life¦100612.
\p
\v 15 Then¦100615 Yahweh¦100616 told¦100615 Yehoshua¦100619,
\v 16 “\add ≈Now order\add* the¦100625 priests¦100625 carrying¦100626 the¦100627 box¦100627 with the¦100628 agreement to come¦100629 up¦100629 out of \add what was\add* the¦100632 Yordan¦100632 \add River\add*,”
\v 17 \add ≈so¦100634\add* Yehoshua¦100635 instructed¦100634 the¦100638 priests¦100638 to¦100639 come¦100640 on up¦100640 from¦100641 the¦100643 Yordan¦100643.
\v 18 As soon as the¦100648 priests¦100648 carrying¦100649 the¦100650 box¦100650 with Yahweh's¦100653 agreement¦100651 came¦100646 up¦100646 out¦100656 of¦100654 \add what had been\add* the¦100655 Yordan¦100655 \add River\add* and their feet¦100658 stepped onto \add what had been\add* dry¦100661 land¦100661, the¦100663 river \add #water¦100663\add* returned¦100662 to¦100666 its place¦100666 and¦100667 overflowed it banks¦100675 as¦100668 \add ≈it had been doing for the previous few days¦100670\add*.
\p
\v 19 The¦100677 people¦100677 had come¦100678 up¦100678 from¦100679 the river valley \add ≈around the end of March\add* and¦100685 they¦100685 camped¦100685 east¦100688 of¦100688 Yeriho¦100689 \add !(Jericho¦100689)\add* at Gilgal¦100686,
\v 20 which¦100696 was \add *where\add* \add #they¦100697\add* had¦100697 set¦100701 up¦100701 the \add monument of\add* twelve boulders¦100694.
\v 21 Then¦100705 \add @Yehoshua¦100705\add* told¦100705 the¦100708 Israelis¦100709, “\add ≈In the future\add* when your¦100713 descendants¦100713 ask¦100718 why these¦100721 boulders¦100720 are here,
\v 22 tell¦100727 them that this¦100734 is where Yisrael¦100730 crossed¦100729 the¦100733 Yordan¦100733 \add River\add* on dry land¦100728.
\v 23 Your god Yahweh¦100739 dried¦100738 up¦100738 the¦100743 river \add #water¦100743\add* ahead¦100745 of¦100745 you¦100745 until¦100746 you'd¦100748 all crossed¦100748 over¦100748, just¦100749 as¦100749 \add *he¦100751\add* had done¦100750 when he¦100758 dried¦100758 up¦100758 the Red Sea¦100753 before¦100759 we¦100762 crossed¦100762 over¦100762.
\v 24 Yahweh did that so¦100764 that all¦100766 the¦100768 peoples¦100768 in the¦100769 world¦100769 would know¦100765 that¦100774 \add *he\add* is¦100775 powerful¦100775, \add and\add* so¦100777 that¦100777 you'll¦100778 always all respect¦100778 \add *him¦100781\add*.
\c 5
\rem /s1 The New Generation Circumcised; Circumcision at Gilgal
\p
\v 1 When¦100788 all¦100790 the Amorite¦100793 kings who¦100794 were¦100795 on¦100795 the¦100795 \add west\add* side¦100795 of¦100795 the¦100796 Yordan¦100796 (towards the ocean) and¦100798 all¦100798 the¦100800 Canaanite¦100801 kings (beside the¦100805 ocean¦100805) heard¦100789 how¦100807 Yahweh¦100810 had¦100809 dried¦100809 up¦100809 the¦100813 \add #water¦100813\add* in the¦100814 Yordan¦100814 \add River\add* until¦100819 \add @the¦100821 Israelis¦100821\add* had¦100821 crossed¦100821 over¦100821, they \add ≈trembled with fear\add* and¦100823 \add ≈lost their¦100824 nerve to stand against\add* Yisrael¦100834.
\s1 Circumcising the males and celebrating ‘pass-over’ at Gilgal
\rem /s1 The Circumcision at Gilgal; Israel Reestablishes Covenant Ceremonies
