\p
\v 2 At¦100837 that¦100838 time¦100837, Yahweh¦100840 told¦100839 Yehoshua¦100843, “Make¦100844 yourself¦100845 flint¦100847 knives¦100846 and¦100848 again circumcise¦100849 the¦100852 male Israelis¦100854.”
\v 3 \add ≈So¦100857\add* Yehoshua¦100860 \add had\add* flint¦100862 knives¦100861 made¦100857 and¦100863 the¦100866 \add male\add* Israelis¦100867 were circumcised¦100863 at \add a place they named\add* ‘The¦100870 hill¦100870 of¦100870 foreskins¦100871’.
\v 4 (This¦100873 was¦100874 done because all¦100879 the¦100881 men¦100881 who'd left¦100892 Egypt¦100883 and who were old enough to join the army \add had been circumcised but\add* had¦100889 died¦100889 in¦100890 the wilderness¦100890 since then¦100892,\x + \xo 5:4: \xt Num 14:28-35.\x*
\v 5 \add and\add* because¦100895 all¦100899 the¦100901 \add ≈boys\add* who'd been¦100898 born¦100906 while they were in¦100907 the wilderness¦100907 after they'd¦100909 left¦100909 Egypt¦100910 hadn't been circumcised¦100913.
\v 6 The Israelis¦100922 had spent forty¦100917 years¦100918 \add ≈moving\add* around the¦100920 wilderness¦100923 until¦100924 the last¦100926 of those men¦100930 who'd¦100932 left¦100932 Egypt¦100933 but hadn't listened¦100937 to¦100938 Yahweh¦100939 \add ≈had died\add*. Yahweh¦100942 had¦100941 promised¦100941 not¦100944 to¦100945 let¦100945 them¦100945 see¦100945 the¦100948 land¦100948 that¦100949 \add *he'd¦100951\add* promised¦100950 to¦100952 their¦100952 ancestors¦100952 to¦100953 give¦100953 \add %them¦100954\add*—a¦100955 land¦100955 flowing¦100956 with milk¦100957 and¦100958 honey¦100958.
\v 7 It was the sons¦100962 of those people¦100975 that Yehoshua¦100967 had circumcised¦100966 \add this time\add* because¦100968 they¦100971 hadn't been¦100971 circumcised¦100975 on¦100977 the way¦100977.)
\p
\v 8 After all¦100983 their males had¦100982 been¦100986 circumcised¦100986, they¦100987 remained in that camp¦100989 until¦100990 they'd¦100991 \add ≈healed up\add*.
\v 9 Then¦100994 Yahweh¦100995 told¦100994 Yehoshua¦100998, “Today I've¦101000 rolled¦101000 away¦101000 the¦101003 disgrace¦101003 of¦101003 Egypt¦101004 from¦101005 you¦101005,” and¦101006 that¦101009 place¦101008 is named¦101007 Gilgal¦101010\f + \fr 5:9 \ft The name ‘Gilgal’ (‘גִּלְגָּל’, ‘circle’) sounds like ‘galal’ (‘גַּלַל’, ‘roll’).\f* until¦101011 this¦101013 day.
\rem /s1 The Passover at Gilgal
\p
\v 10 In¦101028 the evening¦101028 of \add ≈the fourth day¦101026 that the people¦101016 had been camped¦101015\add* at¦101019 Gilgal¦101019 there on the¦101029 plains¦101029 near Yeriho¦101030 \add !(Jericho¦101030)\add*, they celebrated the ‘pass-over¦101023’.\x + \xo 5:10: \xt Exo 12:1-13.\x*
\s1 Eating from the land—no more manna
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 11 The¦101035 next¦101035 day¦101035 they ate roasted¦101038 grain¦101038 that \add they'd taken from that area\add*, and ate flat bread¦101037 that same day¦101040.
\v 12 The day¦101045 after they'd eaten¦101046 some¦101047 of¦101047 the¦101047 produce¦101047 from that area, there was no manna \add on the ground to be collected\add* and \add so\add* it stopped\x + \xo 5:12: \xt Exo 16:35.\x*—instead they'd¦101056 eat¦101056 the¦101057 produce¦101057 from the¦101058 Canaan¦101059 region \add beginning\add* that year¦101060.
\s1 Yehoshua and the man with a sword
\rem /s1 The Lord's Commander Confronts Joshua; Joshua and the Man with a Sword; The Fall of Jericho; Joshua's Vision
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 13 While Yehoshua¦101066 was in the Yeriho¦101067 \add !(Jericho¦101067) area\add*, he¦101068 looked up¦101068 and¦101070 saw¦101070 a¦101073 man¦101073 \add ≈in¦101075 front¦101075 of¦101075\add* him¦101075. The man had drawn¦101077 his¦101076 sword¦101076 and was¦101077 holding it in¦101078 his¦101078 hand¦101078 \add ≈so¦101079\add* Yehoshua¦101080 approached him¦101081 and¦101082 asked¦101082, “Are¦101085 you¦101085 on \em our\em* side, or¦101086 with our¦101088 enemies¦101088?”
\p
\v 14 “No¦101092,” the man \add ≈answered\add*, “but I¦101094, the¦101095 leader of¦101095 Yahweh's¦101099 army¦101097, have¦101101 come¦101101 now¦101100.”
\p Then¦101102 Yehoshua¦101103 fell¦101102 \add ≈to¦101104 his¦101106 knees\add* and¦101108 bowed¦101108 down¦101108 with his face¦101106 to the ground¦101107, and¦101109 \add ≈asked¦101109\add* him¦101110, “What's¦101111 my¦101112 master¦101112 going to \add ≈command\add* to his¦101116 servant¦101116?”
\p
\v 15 “Take¦101126 off¦101126 your \add #sandals¦101128\add*,” the¦101119 commander¦101119 of¦101119 Yahweh's¦101122 army¦101121 told¦101118 \add *him¦101125\add*, “because¦101131 the¦101132 ground that¦101133 you're¦101134 standing¦101135 is¦101137 holy¦101137.” \add ≈So¦101139\add* Yehoshua¦101140 \add ≈took them off\add*.
\c 6
\s1 Yeriho's walls collapse
\rem /s1 Jericho Taken and Destroyed; The Fall of Jericho
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 1 \add ≈Now\add* Yeriho¦101143 \add !(Jericho¦101143) city\add* was¦101144 shut-up tightly \add ≈because of¦101146 the¦101147 Israelis¦101148\add*, \add so\add* no one was¦101149 coming¦101150 out¦101150 and¦101151 no one could go¦101150 in.
\v 2 Then¦101155 Yahweh¦101156 told¦101155 Yehoshua¦101159, “Listen, I've¦101161 given¦101161 you \add ≈victory over\add* Yeriho¦101165 and¦101166 its¦101168 king¦101168, and \add ≈their\add* mighty¦101169 army \add >warriors\add*.
\v 3 All¦101176 your soldiers must¦101172 go¦101172 around¦101172 the¦101175 city¦101175 once every¦101176 day for six¦101187 days¦101188
\v 4 with seven¦101190 priests¦101191 \add ≈blowing\add* ram's horns¦101195 going ahead of¦101196 the¦101197 \add sacred\add* box¦101197. On¦101198 the¦101199 seventh¦101199 day¦101198, you¦101200 all must¦101200 go¦101200 around¦101200 the¦101203 city¦101203 seven¦101204 times¦101205 while the¦101206 priests¦101206 are blowing¦101207 the horns¦101208.
\v 5 \add ≈Finally,\add* with a long blast¦101211 of¦101213 the¦101214 horn¦101214, when¦101211 you¦101215 all hear¦101215 that then all¦101222 the¦101224 people¦101224 must¦101221 shout¦101225 loudly¦101226 and¦101227 the¦101228 wall¦101228 around the¦101229 city¦101229 will¦101227 fall¦101227 down flat, and¦101231 all the¦101232 \add ≈soldiers\add* should go¦101231 straight in \add from where they're standing\add*.”
\p
\v 6 \add ≈So¦101236\add* Yehoshua¦101237 summoned¦101236 the¦101243 priests¦101243 and¦101244 told¦101244 them¦101245, “Carry¦101253 the¦101249 box¦101249 with the¦101250 agreement¦101250, and¦101251 have seven¦101251 priests¦101252 hold up¦101246 seven¦101254 rams' horns¦101256 \add ≈ahead¦101257\add* of¦101258 Yahweh's¦101259 box.”
\v 7 Then¦101261 he¦101261 told¦101261 the¦101265 people¦101265, “Go¦101266 across in¦101273 front¦101273 and¦101267 go¦101267 around¦101267 the¦101270 city¦101270, \add ≈with the soldiers going ahead¦101273\add* of¦101274 Yahweh's¦101275 box¦101274.”
\p
\v 8 After¦101298 Yehoshua¦101279 had¦101278 spoken¦101278 to¦101280 the¦101282 people¦101282, the seven priests¦101284 with their seven¦101286 rams' horns¦101288 went¦101297 across in¦101289 front¦101289 and¦101292 blew¦101292 the horns¦101293, and¦101294 the¦101294 box¦101294 with Yahweh's¦101296 covenant¦101295 was \add ≈carried¦101285\add* along behind them.
\v 9 The¦101300 \add ≈soldiers\add* walked¦101301 ahead of¦101302 the¦101303 priests¦101303 blowing¦101304 the¦101306 horns¦101306, with the¦101307 rear guard¦101307 walking¦101308 behind¦101309 the¦101310 box¦101310. \add So\add* they were walking¦101311 and¦101312 blowing the horns¦101313,
\v 10 and¦101315 Yehoshua¦101319 told the¦101317 people¦101317, “Don't¦101321 shout¦101322 \add ≈or even speak¦101332 or make¦101325 a¦101333 noise\add* until¦101334 the¦101335 day¦101335 I¦101336 tell you all to shout¦101338—then¦101339 you¦101339 all should shout¦101339 loudly.”
\p
\v 11 \add ≈So¦101341\add* Yahweh's¦101344 box¦101342 was carried once around¦101341 the¦101347 city¦101347, then¦101351 the people went¦101351 back to the¦101352 camp¦101352 and¦101353 stayed¦101353 the night there.
\p
\v 12 Yehoshua¦101358 got up early¦101357 the next morning¦101359, and¦101360 the¦101361 priests¦101361 picked up Yahweh's¦101365 box¦101364
\v 13 and¦101367 the seven priests¦101368 holding the seven rams' horns¦101372 went in¦101373 front¦101373 of¦101373 \add *it\add*—blowing the horns as they¦101378 kept walking. The¦101380 \add ≈soldiers\add* walking¦101381 in¦101382 front¦101382 of¦101382 them¦101382, and¦101383 the¦101383 rear guard¦101383 walked¦101384 behind¦101385 Yahweh's¦101387 box \add ≈while\add* the horns¦101391 were being blown.
\v 14 They¦101393 went¦101393 once around¦101393 the¦101396 city¦101396 on that second¦101398 day¦101397 and¦101401 then returned¦101401 to \add &their¦101402\add* camp¦101402 \add again\add*—doing¦101404 that for six¦101405 days¦101406.
\p
\v 15 Then¦101408 on the¦101411 seventh¦101411 day they¦101412 got up¦101413 early¦101412 at dawn¦101414 and¦101415 went¦101415 around¦101415 the¦101418 city¦101418 \add ≈as before\add*, except this¦101420 day¦101424 they¦101426 went¦101426 around¦101426 seven¦101430 times¦101431.
\v 16 \add ≈After that seventh¦101435 time¦101434 around,\add* the¦101437 priests¦101437 blew¦101436 \add a long blast\add* on¦101438 the rams' horns¦101438 and¦101439 Yehoshua¦101440 told¦101439 the¦101443 people¦101443, “Shout¦101444, because¦101445 Yahweh¦101448 has¦101447 given¦101447 you¦101449 all the¦101452 city¦101452!
\v 17 \add However,\add* everything in the¦101455 city¦101455 is¦101462 sacred to¦101463 Yahweh¦101463. Only¦101464 the¦101466 prostitute¦101466 Rahab¦101465 and¦101469 those who¦101471 are¦101472 in her¦101472 house¦101473 will be allowed to live¦101467, because¦101474 she¦101475 hid¦101475 the¦101478 spies that¦101460 we¦101480 sent¦101480 in.
\v 18 But¦101482 for all of you¦101484, everything inside the¦101488 city is forbidden—if any¦101493 of you take¦101492 anything out of¦101493 the¦101495 city then¦101496 our camp¦101499 \add ≈would also then be marked for destruction¦101491\add* and¦101502 it would¦101502 cause¦101496 \add a lot of\add* trouble¦101502.
\v 19 All¦101505 the silver¦101507 and¦101508 gold¦101508, bronze¦101510 and¦101511 iron¦101511 is¦101512 dedicated¦101512 to¦101514 Yahweh and must¦101517 go¦101517 into \add *his\add* treasury¦101515.
\p
\v 20 \add ≈So¦101519\add* the¦101520 people¦101520 shouted¦101519 when¦101521 that horn¦101529 blew¦101521—as soon as they heard¦101524 \add *it\add* the¦101525 people¦101525 shouted¦101530 loudly¦101533 and¦101534 the¦101535 wall¦101535 fell¦101534 down on itself\x + \xo 6:20: \xt Heb 11:30.\x* and¦101537 the¦101538 people¦101538 went up \add and over\add* into¦101539 the¦101539 city¦101539 from wherever they were standing and captured¦101542 the¦101545 city¦101545.
\v 21 They¦101547 \add ≈killed\add* every¦101550 \add living thing\add* in¦101553 the city¦101553 with \add &their\add* \add #swords¦101568\add*, including men¦101554 and¦101555 \add #women¦101557\add*, young¦101558 and¦101559 old¦101561, even cattle¦101563, sheep¦101564, and¦101565 donkeys¦101565.
\p
\v 22 Then¦101570 Yehoshua¦101577 commanded the two¦101570 men¦101571 who¦101572 had¦101572 spied¦101572 on the¦101575 area, “Go¦101578 to the¦101582 prostitute's¦101582 house¦101579 and¦101583 bring¦101583 the¦101587 woman¦101587 out of it and¦101588 all¦101590 who¦101592 are related to¦101594 her¦101594, just¦101595 as¦101595 you¦101596 promised¦101596 her¦101597.”
\v 23 \add ≈So¦101599\add* the¦101600 young¦101600 men¦101600 \add ≈who'd¦101601 gone in as\add* spies¦101601 went¦101599 in and¦101602 brought¦101602 out¦101602 Rahab¦101605 and¦101606 her¦101608 parents¦101611 and all¦101623 her¦101625 relatives¦101614 and¦101627 settled them¦101627 outside¦101628 of¦101629 the¦101629 camp¦101629 of the Israelis¦101630.
\v 24 Then¦101632 \add @the warriors\add* set fire¦101634 to the¦101632 city¦101632 and burnt¦101633 everything that¦101637 was¦101639 in¦101639 it¦101639. Only¦101640 the¦101642 silver¦101642 and¦101643 gold¦101643, and¦101644 bronze¦101645 and¦101646 iron¦101646 were \add first removed and\add* put¦101647 into the¦101648 treasury¦101648 of¦101648 Yahweh's¦101651 house¦101649.
\v 25 \add ≈But¦101653\add* Yehoshua spared the¦101656 prostitute¦101656 Rahab¦101655 and¦101657 her¦101660 father's¦101660 household¦101659 and¦101661 her¦101667 other relatives because¦101676 she¦101677 hid¦101677 the¦101680 men that Yehoshua¦101684 had¦101683 sent¦101683 in to¦101685 spy¦101685 on Yeriho¦101688 \add !(Jericho¦101688)\add*,\x + \xo 6:25: \xt Heb 11:31.\x* and she still lives¦101668 in¦101671 Yisrael¦101672 to this¦101675 day¦101674.
\p
\v 26 At¦101693 that time¦101693, Yehoshua¦101692 made \add @the people\add* take an¦101691 oath¦101691, saying¦101695,
\q1 “May Yahweh¦101699 curse¦101696 anyone who¦101700 rebuilds¦101702 this¦101706 city¦101705, Yeriho¦101709 \add !(Jericho¦101709)\add*.
\q1 When that person¦101697 lays its \add ≈foundation¦101711\add*, may his¦101712 oldest son¦101712 die.
\q1 And when he¦101713 \add finishes building the city wall and\add* sets¦101713 up¦101713 its¦101714 gates¦101714, may his youngest¦101712 son die.”\x + \xo 6:26: \xt 1Ki 16:34.\x*
\p
\v 27 \add ≈So¦101716\add* Yahweh¦101717 was with¦101718 Yehoshua¦101720 and¦101721 \add ≈everyone¦101723 in that region¦101725 had heard about¦101722 him¦101722\add*.
\c 7
\s1 Achan's sin
\rem /s1 Ai Defeats the Israelites; The Sin of Achan and Its Punishment; Achan's Sin
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 1 \add ≈However\add* the¦101728 Israelis¦101730 disobeyed the command about \add ≈not taking anything\add*. Achan¦101734 (son¦101735 of¦101735 Karmi¦101737, son¦101738 of¦101738 Zabdi¦101740, son¦101741 of¦101741 Zerah¦101743, from the¦101744 tribe¦101744 of¦101744 Yehudah¦101745) took¦101733 something that was prohibited, \add ≈so¦101749\add* Yahweh¦101752 \add ≈was angry¦101751\add* with the¦101753 Israelis¦101754.
\p
\v 2 \add ≈Meanwhile,\add* Yehoshua¦101757 sent¦101756 some of his men¦101758 from¦101759 Yeriho¦101759 \add !(Jericho¦101759)\add* to Ay¦101760 (east¦101766 of¦101767 Beyt¦101767-El¦101769 and near Beyt¦101764-Aven¦101765) and¦101770 told¦101770 them¦101771, “Go¦101773 \add ≈to Ay\add* and¦101774 spy¦101774 out¦101774 the¦101777 land¦101777.” \add ≈So¦101778\add* the¦101779 men¦101779 went¦101778 and¦101780 checkout out¦101780 Ay¦101783.
\v 3 \add ≈When¦101785\add* they¦101785 returned¦101785 to¦101786 Yehoshua¦101788, they¦101789 told¦101789 him¦101790, “Don't¦101791 \add ≈send all¦101794 the¦101796 warriors\add*—\add only\add* around¦101797 two¦101797 to three¦101800 thousand¦101801 men¦101802 should¦101803 go¦101803 and¦101804 attack¦101804 them. Don't¦101808 \add ≈bother everyone else\add* because¦101818 \add ≈Ay¦101807 is¦101819 small\add*.”
\v 4 \add ≈So¦101822\add* around¦101827 three¦101827 thousand¦101828 \add ≈warriors¦101832\add* went¦101822 to¦101826 \add attack Ay, but they were defeated\add* and¦101830 had to¦101831 flee¦101830 \add back\add*.
\v 5 The¦101837 men¦101837 from Ay¦101838 chased¦101842 them¦101842 from the \add city\add* gate¦101844 downhill to¦101845 Shevarim¦101847 and¦101848 fought them¦101848 on the¦101851 slopes. About¦101851 thirty-six \add ≈of¦101853 them\add* were killed, and the¦101853 \add ≈Israelis¦101853 became very afraid and¦101854 lost all their courage¦101851\add*.
\p
