\v 30 It¦105857 went from¦105859 Mahanaim¦105859, all¦105860 the¦105862 Bashan¦105862, all¦105863 the¦105865 kingdom¦105865 of¦105865 Og¦105867 (the¦105868 king¦105868 of¦105868 the¦105870 Bashan¦105870), and¦105871 all¦105871 the¦105873 towns of¦105873 Yair¦105874, which¦105875 are¦105876 in¦105876 the Bashan¦105876—sixty¦105877 cities¦105878.
\v 31 \add ≈Also¦105880\add* half¦105880 of¦105880 the¦105881 Gilead¦105881, plus¦105882 Ashtaroth¦105882 and¦105883 Edrei¦105883 (cities¦105884 of¦105884 the¦105885 kingdom¦105885 of¦105885 Og¦105886 in¦105887 the Bashan¦105887). So that was for half of¦105888 Machir's¦105889 sons¦105890 (\add *he\add* was one of¦105890 Menashsheh's¦105892 \add #sons\add*) allocated to their¦105897 clans¦105897.
\p
\v 32 This was¦105900 the land that¦105900 Mosheh¦105903 gave¦105902 as¦105902 an inheritance in¦105904 the¦105904 plains¦105904 of¦105904 Moab¦105905 on the¦105906 eastern¦105909 side¦105906 of¦105907 the¦105907 Yordan¦105907 \add River opposite\add* Yeriho¦105908 \add !(Jericho¦105908)\add*.
\v 33 \add ≈However,\add* Mosheh¦105917 didn't¦105914 give¦105916 any inheritance¦105918 \add of land\add* to Levi's descendants \add because\add* Yisrael's¦105921 god¦105920 Yahweh¦105919 is¦105923 their¦105923 inheritance just¦105924 as¦105924 he¦105925 told¦105925 them¦105926.\x + \xo 13:33: \xt Num 18:20; Deu 18:2.\x*
\c 14
