\v 2 Their¦105953 \add ≈allocations were made by¦105957 casting lots\add* for¦105960 the¦105960 nine¦105960 and¦105962 a half¦105962 tribes¦105963, just¦105954 as¦105954 Yahweh¦105956 had¦105955 commanded¦105955 \add ≈through\add* Mosheh¦105959.\x + \xo 14:2: \xt Num 26:52-56; 34:13.\x*
\v 3 (Mosheh¦105968 had¦105967 given¦105967 the¦105969 other two¦105970 and¦105972 a half¦105972 tribes¦105973 their inheritance on the¦105974 other¦105974 side¦105974 of¦105975 the river,\x + \xo 14:3-4: \xt Num 32:33; 34:14-15; Deu 3:12-17.\x* but¦105976 the Levites¦105976 weren't given¦105979 land as an¦105980 inheritance¦105980—
\v 4 ⇔instead of land¦106004 they were given¦105995 cities¦106002 to¦106003 live¦106003 in¦106003, along with the \add surrounding\add* fields for¦106005 their¦106005 livestock¦106005. Yosef's¦105988 two¦105989 sons Menashsheh¦105991 and¦105992 Efrayim¦105992 were considered as two tribes¦105990.)
\v 5 The¦106016 \add ≈Israelis¦106017\add* did just¦106008 as¦106008 Yahweh¦106010 had¦106009 commanded¦106009 Mosheh¦106013—they¦106015 allocated blocks of the¦106021 land¦106021 \add as permanent possessions\add*.
\s1 Hebron is allocated to Caleb
\rem /s1 Hebron Allotted to Caleb; Caleb Requests His Land; Hebron Is Given to Caleb; Hebron Given to Caleb
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 6 \add ≈Leaders from the¦106025 tribe of¦106025\add* Yehudah¦106027 approached¦106024 Yehoshua¦106030 at¦106031 Gilgal¦106031 and¦106032 Caleb¦106034 (son¦106035 of¦106035 Yefunneh¦106037 the¦106038 Kenizzite¦106038) said¦106032 to¦106033 him¦106033, “You yourself know¦106040 what Yahweh¦106047 told¦106046 the¦106051 man¦106051 of¦106051 God Mosheh¦106050 at¦106058 Kadesh¦106058-Barnea¦106059 about me and you.\x + \xo 14:6: \xt Num 14:30.\x*
\v 7 I was¦106061 \add ≈forty¦106063 years¦106064 old\add* when¦106066 Yahweh's¦106070 servant¦106068 Mosheh¦106067 sent¦106066 me¦106071 from¦106072 Kadesh¦106072-Barnea¦106073 to¦106074 spy¦106074 out¦106074 the¦106077 land¦106077, and¦106078 I¦106078 brought¦106078 back¦106078 \add ≈an honest report\add*.\x + \xo 14:7: \xt Num 13:1-30.\x*
\v 8 \add ≈The other men\add* who¦106087 went¦106088 made the \add ≈people¦106094 terrified\add*, \add ≈but¦106095\add* I \add ≈remained loyal to\add* my¦106099 god¦106099 Yahweh¦106098.
\v 9 Mosheh¦106102 \add ≈promised¦106101 me\add* that day¦106103, saying¦106105, ‘The¦106109 land¦106109 \add ≈that¦106110 you walked on¦106113\add* will¦106115 certainly be for an¦106116 inheritance¦106116 for you and¦106117 your¦106117 sons¦106117 \add ≈forever¦106120\add*, because¦106121 you¦106122 were \add ≈completely loyal to\add* my¦106125 god¦106125 Yahweh¦106124.’\x + \xo 14:9: \xt Num 14:24.\x*
\v 10 Now¦106127, listen. Yahweh¦106130 has kept me¦106132 alive¦106129 these forty-five years¦106138 since Yahweh¦106141 said¦106140 that¦106145 to¦106146 Mosheh¦106148, \add back\add* when¦106149 Yisrael¦106152 was walking¦106151 in¦106153 the wilderness¦106153. \add ≈Yes, believe it or not, I'm now¦106154 eighty-five.\add*
\v 11 I'm still¦106164 as strong¦106166 today as¦106167 \add I was\add* on¦106168 the day¦106168 that Mosheh¦106171 sent¦106169 me¦106170. \add ≈Just like¦106172 I could fight back then¦106173, I can still fight¦106176 or travel¦106177 just the same\add*.
\v 12 \add ≈So¦106180\add* now¦106180, please give¦106181 me¦106183 that hill¦106186 country¦106186 that¦106188 Yahweh¦106191 \add ≈promised\add* that day, because¦106194 you yourself heard¦106197 \add ≈me say\add* that the Anakim¦106202 lived there¦106203 in fortified¦106206 cities¦106204. \add So now,\add* perhaps¦106207 Yahweh¦106208 will¦106209 help me¦106209 to take them¦106210 over just¦106211 as¦106211 \add *he¦106213\add* said¦106212.”
\p
\v 13 \add ≈So¦106215\add* Yehoshua¦106216 blessed¦106215 Yefunneh's¦106224 son¦106222 \add @Caleb¦106215\add* and¦106217 gave¦106217 him Hebron¦106220 as his inheritance¦106225.
\v 14 Because of that¦106243, Hebron¦106232 belongs¦106230 to¦106233 Caleb¦106233 (Yefunneh¦106236 the¦106237 Kenizzite's¦106237 son¦106234) as an¦106238 inheritance¦106238 until¦106239 this¦106241 day¦106240, because¦106242 he¦106244 was \add ≈completely loyal to\add* Yisrael's¦106248 god¦106247 Yahweh¦106246.
\v 15 (Hebron¦106251 used to be¦106253 called¦106250 Kiriat¦106253-Arba¦106254—\add @Arba\add* had been a \add ≈brave warrior\add* among¦106257 the Anakim¦106257.)
\p Then¦106259 there was¦106260 a time of no more war¦106261 in that region.
