\v 6 and¦107042 out¦107042 to¦107044 the \add ≈Mediterranean\add*. From¦107046 Mikmetat in the¦107046 north¦107046, the¦107048 border¦107048 went¦107042 eastward¦107049 toward Taanat-Shiloh¦107051 then¦107052 further east¦107054 to¦107055 Yanoah¦107055.
\v 7 From¦107058 Yanoah¦107058 it went to Atarot¦107059 and¦107060 Naarah¦107060, reached¦107061 Yeriho¦107062 \add !(Jericho¦107062)\add* then¦107063 came out¦107063 at the¦107064 Yordan¦107064.
\v 8 \add The northern border went\add* from¦107066 Tappuah¦107066 to¦107069 the¦107070 Kanah¦107071 riverbed¦107070 and¦107072 then out to¦107074 the¦107074 \add ≈Mediterranean\add*. That¦107075 was¦107076 the¦107076 inheritance¦107076 of Efrayim's¦107080 descendants¦107078 according to¦107081 their¦107081 clans¦107081,
\v 9 \add ≈although\add* some of the¦107083 cities¦107083 with their¦107095 villages¦107095 for¦107085 Efrayim's¦107086 descendants were \add actually\add* inside the territory assigned to Menashsheh's¦107091 descendants.
\v 10 \add ≈But¦107097\add* they¦107098 didn't¦107097 \add ≈capture the land of\add* the¦107101 Canaanites¦107101 who¦107102 lived¦107102 in¦107103 Gezer¦107103, so¦107104 they've lived¦107104 within¦107106 Efrayim¦107107 to this¦107111 day¦107110 and¦107112 were¦107112 forced to¦107113 serve as labourers¦107115.\x + \xo 16:10: \xt Jdg 1:29.\x*
\c 17
\s1 The allocation to Menashsheh's descendants
\rem /s1 The Land Given to West Manasseh; West Manasseh; The Other Half-Tribe of Manasseh (West)
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 1 The allotment for Menashsheh's¦107121 descendants (Yosef's¦107126 eldest¦107128 son) \add included a special allotment for\add* (Gilead's¦107131 father¦107130) Makir¦107127—he was given Gilead¦107140 and¦107141 Bashan¦107141 because he was a \add ≈powerful warrior\add*.
\v 2 The¦107144 other Menashsheh¦107145 clans¦107147 \add that were allocated land\add* were the¦107148 Abiezer¦107149, Helek¦107152, Asriel¦107154, Shekem¦107157, Hefer¦107160, and¦107161 Shemida¦107162 clans. (They were¦107164 the sons¦107166 of¦107166 Yosef's¦107168 son Menashsheh \add who led their own\add* clans¦107170.)
\v 3 \add ≈But¦107172\add* Zelofehad¦107172 (son¦107173 of¦107173 Hefer¦107175, son¦107176 of¦107176 Gilead¦107178, son¦107179 of¦107179 Makir¦107181, son¦107182 of¦107182 Menashsheh¦107184) had no sons¦107189—only daughters¦107193 who were¦107195 named¦107195 Mahlah¦107197, Noah¦107198, Hoglah¦107199, Milkah¦107200, and¦107201 Tirzah¦107201.
\v 4 They¦107203 approached¦107203 the¦107204 priest¦107206 Eleazar¦107205 and¦107207 Yehoshua¦107209 and¦107213 the¦107214 other leaders¦107214 and said¦107215, “Yahweh¦107216 told¦107217 Mosheh¦107220 to¦107221 give¦107221 us¦107223 an¦107224 inheritance¦107224 along with our¦107226 brothers.” \add ≈So¦107227\add* he¦107227\f + \fr 17:4 \ft It's not clear who this ‘he’ refers to here—some translations choose Eleazar (implied by the sentence structure) and others choose Yehoshua (implied by past allocations of land).\f* gave¦107227 them¦107228 an¦107233 inheritance¦107233 (like he'd given their¦107236 uncles), as Yahweh \add ≈had instructed them\add*.\x + \xo 17:4: \xt Num 27:1-7.\x*
\v 5 \add ≈So¦107238\add* ten¦107242 blocks were allocated to Menashsheh¦107241 \add tribe\add* as well as Gilead¦107245 and¦107246 Bashan¦107246 which¦107247 were¦107248 across the¦107248 Yordan¦107249
\v 6 because¦107251 Menashsheh's¦107253 daughters¦107252 received \add #inheritances¦107255\add* along with his¦107257 sons. The¦107258 land¦107258 of¦107258 Gilead¦107259 belonged¦107260 to¦107261 the¦107261 rest¦107264 of¦107261 Menashsheh's¦107263 sons.
\p
\v 7 The¦107267 border¦107267 for Menashsheh¦107269 went from¦107270 Asher¦107270 to Mikmetat \add ≈opposite\add* Shekem¦107276, then¦107277 went¦107277 \add ≈south¦107281\add* towards the¦107284 spring at Tappuah.
\v 8 (The¦107290 Tappuah¦107291 \em land¦107290\em* was for Menashsheh, but¦107292 Tappuah¦107292 \add town\add* was for Efrayim¦107298.)
\v 9 Then¦107300 the¦107301 border¦107301 went¦107300 south¦107304 to¦107304 the¦107304 Kanah¦107303 riverbed¦107305—the cities there belonged¦107308 to¦107308 Efrayim¦107308 even though they were inside Menashsheh's¦107311 land—then¦107312 the¦107312 border¦107312 stayed on the¦107314 north¦107314 side of¦107314 the riverbed¦107315 and¦107316 extended to¦107318 the¦107318 \add ≈Mediterranean\add*.
\v 10 \add So\add* the south¦107320 was for Efrayim¦107321 and¦107322 the north¦107322 was for Menashsheh¦107323, and¦107324 the¦107325 sea¦107325 was the \add western\add* border¦107326, meeting Asher¦107327 from¦107329 the¦107329 north¦107329 and¦107330 Yissakar¦107330 from¦107331 the¦107331 east¦107331.
\v 11 Menashsheh¦107334 was allocated \add cities\add* inside \add both\add* Yissakar's¦107335 and¦107336 Asher's¦107336 \add territories\add*: Beyt¦107337-Shan¦107339, Ibleam¦107341, Dor¦107346, Endor¦107351, Taanach¦107354, and Megiddo¦107357 along with their \add ≈surrounding towns\add*.\f + \fr 17:11 \ft We've omitted the final Hebrew phrase here (the three of Nafet) since it's unclear what it means (plus it's not considered to be a vital point in the narrative).\f*
\v 12 \add ≈But¦107362\add* Menashsheh's¦107365 descendants¦107364 weren't able¦107363 to¦107366 take¦107366 possession¦107366 of¦107366 those¦107370 cities¦107369, \add ≈so¦107371\add* the¦107372 Canaanites¦107372 continued to¦107373 live¦107373 in the region.\x + \xo 17:12-13: \xt Jdg 1:27-28.\x*
\v 13 \add ≈When¦107377 the¦107380 Israelis¦107381 strengthened¦107379 their position\add*, they¦107382 were able to¦107386 force¦107386 those Canaanites to work¦107386 for them, \add ≈but¦107387\add* they weren't able to \add ≈drive them out\add*.
\s1 Efrayim and Menashsheh's descendants are given additional land
\rem /s1 The Tribe of Joseph Protests; Ephraim and West Manasseh Request More Land
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 14 Then¦107392 the¦107393 \add two\add* \add ≈half-tribes of¦107393 Efrayim and Menashsheh\add* asked¦107398 Yehoshua¦107397, “Why¦107399 have¦107400 you¦107400 \add only\add* given¦107400 to¦107401 \add #us\add* one measured allocation as an¦107402 inheritance¦107402 when \add #we're\add* \add very\add* numerous¦107410 \add because\add* Yahweh¦107418 has¦107417 \add ≈already\add* blessed¦107417 \add #us\add*?”
\p
\v 15 “If \add ≈there's so¦107420 many of you\add*,” Yehoshua¦107422 \add ≈answered¦107420\add*, “and if¦107423 Efrayim's¦107444 hill-country is¦107425 too small for you¦107428, go¦107429 into the¦107431 forested¦107431 area¦107442 of¦107436 the¦107436 Perizzites and¦107437 the¦107437 Refaites¦107437 and clear some land¦107435 for¦107441 yourselves there.”
\p
\v 16 “The¦107447 hill¦107453 country¦107453 \add certainly\add* isn't¦107449 big enough for¦107452 \add all of\add* us¦107452,” \add *they\add* responded¦107446, “plus¦107454 the¦107458 Canaanites living¦107459 in¦107460 the¦107462 Yezreel¦107470 valley¦107462 and in Beyt-Shan and the¦107469 surrounding towns have iron¦107455 chariots¦107454.”
\p
\v 17 \add ≈So¦107472\add* Yehoshua¦107473 told¦107472 the¦107476 \add ≈half-tribes of¦107476 Efrayim¦107478 and¦107479 Menashsheh¦107479\add*, “\add Yes\add*, there's a¦107481 lot¦107492 of you¦107484 and¦107485 you're very powerful. One¦107493 land allotment \add ≈wouldn't be enough for¦107487 you¦107487\add*
\v 18 \add ≈so\add* the¦107496 hill¦107496 country¦107496 will¦107497 be¦107502 yours \add as well\add*. \add ≈However\add*, it's a forest¦107502 and¦107504 you'll¦107504 have to clear it to¦107506 the borders¦107507. You'll¦107510 \add need to\add* drive¦107510 out the¦107513 Canaanites¦107513 even if they are¦107519 strong¦107519 and with iron¦107516 chariots¦107515.”
\c 18
\s1 Allocations for the remaining seven tribes
\rem /s1 The Territories of the Remaining Tribes; Division of the Rest of the Land; The Allotments of the Remaining Land; The Division of the Rest of the Land
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 1 Then¦107523 all¦107524 the Israelis¦107529 assembled¦107523 at Shiloh¦107530 and¦107531 set up the¦107535 \add sacred\add* tent¦107535 there¦107532. The \add ≈battles over the land¦107537 had stopped\add*
\v 2 but¦107541 seven¦107551 of¦107542 \add *their¦107543\add* tribes¦107552 hadn't had¦107547 their¦107550 \add #inheritances¦107550\add* assigned \add yet\add*.
\v 3 Yehoshua¦107555 asked¦107554 the¦107558 Israelis¦107559, “\add ≈How much longer are¦107564 you¦107563 all going¦107565 to¦107566 put off capturing\add* the¦107569 land¦107569 that¦107570 your¦107575 ancestors¦107575' God¦107574 Yahweh¦107573 has¦107571 given¦107571 you¦107572?
\v 4 Choose three¦107579 men¦107580 from each \add of those seven\add*\f + \fr 18:4 \ft Not in the Hebrew but implied by verse 5 as they go on to divide the surveyed land into seven portions.\f* tribes¦107581 and I'll¦107582 send¦107582 them¦107582 out to \add ≈scout around\add* \add and inspect\add* the¦107585 land¦107585 and¦107586 write¦107586 \add ≈descriptions¦107586 of it in terms of potential allocations and¦107590 bring it\add* to¦107591 me¦107591.
\v 5 They¦107593 can divide¦107593 \add @that¦107594 land¦107594\add* into¦107595 seven¦107595 parts¦107596. (Yehudah¦107597 will¦107598 maintain their territory¦107601 in the¦107602 south¦107602, and¦107603 Yosef's¦107604 tribes in the¦107609 north¦107609.)
\v 6 You all should write¦107612 \add ≈descriptions¦107612\add* of the¦107615 seven¦107616 parts¦107617 and¦107618 bring¦107618 them here¦107624 to¦107619 me¦107619, and in¦107625 front¦107625 of¦107625 our¦107627 god¦107627 Yahweh¦107626, I'll¦107621 throw¦107621 dice for¦107622 you¦107622 \add to allocate them to the seven tribes\add*.
\v 7 However, the Levites¦107633 don't¦107630 receive a¦107632 portion¦107632, because¦107635 their inheritance is¦107637 Yahweh's¦107638 priesthood¦107637. Gad¦107640 and¦107641 Reuven¦107641 and¦107642 the Menashsheh¦107644 half-tribe have¦107645 \add already\add* received¦107645 their inheritance that¦107650 Yahweh's servant¦107654 Mosheh¦107653 allocated to¦107652 them¦107652 on the¦107654 eastern¦107649 side¦107647 of¦107654 the Yordan¦107648.
\p
\v 8 \add ≈So¦107657\add* the¦107658 \add chosen\add* men¦107658 \add ≈got ready to leave\add* and¦107659 Yehoshua¦107661 instructed¦107660 them¦107664, “Go¦107670 and¦107671 walk¦107671 around¦107671 that land¦107672 and¦107673 write¦107673 \add a report\add* and \add ≈bring it back\add* to¦107676 me¦107676. Then¦107677 I'll¦107678 throw¦107678 dice for¦107679 you¦107679 all \add ≈in¦107681 front¦107681\add* of¦107681 Yahweh¦107682 here¦107677 in¦107683 Shiloh¦107683.”
\v 9 Then¦107685 the¦107686 men¦107686 left¦107685 and¦107687 \add ≈walked¦107687 through the¦107688 area\add*, writing¦107689 down \add their recommendations\add* for dividing the seven¦107691 portions¦107692 according to the cities¦107690 \add in the area\add*, then¦107696 they¦107696 returned¦107696 back to¦107697 Yehoshua¦107699 at the¦107702 camp¦107702 at Shiloh¦107703.
\v 10 \add ≈So¦107705\add* Yehoshua threw¦107705 dice for¦107706 them¦107706 at Shiloh¦107709 \add ≈in¦107710 front¦107710\add* of¦107710 Yahweh¦107711, and¦107712 \add ≈so that land¦107718 was allocated to those remaining seven tribes\add*.
\s1 The allocation to Benyamin's descendants
\rem /s1 The Land Given to Benjamin; The Territory of Benjamin; Allotment for Benjamin; The Territory Assigned to Benjamin
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 11 The¦107726 tribe¦107726 of¦107726 Benyamin¦107729 won the \add first\add* draw and¦107731 the¦107732 area for their¦107733 clans¦107730 was between¦107734 the¦107735 land assigned to Yehudah¦107736 and that assigned to \add ≈Efrayim and Menashsheh\add*.
\v 12 Their northern border¦107743 went from¦107746 the¦107748 Yordan¦107748 then¦107749 to¦107751 the¦107753 northern side¦107744 of¦107753 Yeriho¦107754 \add !(Jericho¦107754)\add* and¦107756 up¦107756 into¦107757 the hill country¦107757 to¦107758 the west¦107758, coming out in the¦107762 wilderness¦107762 at Beyt¦107763-Aven¦107764.
\v 13 Then¦107766 it¦107766 went¦107766 across towards Luz (\add ≈now called\add* Beyt¦107776-El¦107778) to the¦107780 southern edge then downhill towards Atarot¦107781-Addar¦107782 beside the¦107785 hill¦107785 south¦107787 of¦107788 lower¦107791 Beyt¦107788-Horon¦107790.
\v 14 Then¦107793 the¦107794 western border¦107794 turned¦107795 from¦107800 that¦107803 hill¦107802 and went south¦107810, coming out at Kiriat¦107816-Baal¦107818 (\add ≈also called\add* Kiriat¦107820-Yearim¦107821—a town¦107822 belonging to Yehudah¦107824) thus forming the¦107826 western side¦107826.
\v 15 The¦107830 southern¦107832 border¦107837 went¦107836 west¦107838 from¦107833 Kiriat¦107835-Yearim to¦107840 the¦107842 spring¦107842 at Neftoah,
\v 16 then¦107846 downhill to¦107848 the Ben¦107856-Hinnon valley¦107859 (in¦107861 the¦107861 valley¦107861 of¦107861 the Refaites¦107862 to the north¦107863) then¦107864 downhill to Hinnon valley¦107865 to¦107867 the¦107869 edge of¦107869 the¦107870 Yebusites¦107870 and downhill to Eyn¦107873-Rogel¦107874.
\v 17 Then¦107876 it¦107876 turned¦107876 northward¦107877 and¦107878 went¦107878 \add west\add* to Eyn¦107879-Shemesh¦107880 and¦107881 across to¦107882 Gelilot¦107884 opposite¦107887 the¦107888 Adummim¦107889 pass, before going¦107890 downhill to the¦107891 Stone¦107891 of¦107891 Bohan¦107893 (Reuben's¦107895 son¦107895).
\v 18 It¦107897 extended over to¦107898 the¦107900 northern¦107904 slope¦107900 of¦107900 the¦107903 Yordan valley and¦107905 then downhill into¦107906 the¦107906 \add actual\add* valley.
\v 19 \add *It\add* then¦107908 went¦107908 \add east\add* to¦107910 the¦107912 northern slope¦107912 of¦107912 Beyt¦107913-Hoglah¦107915 before coming out at¦107929 the¦107932 \add ≈north end¦107932\add* of¦107925 the¦107926 \add ≈Dead Sea¦107926\add* \add (also called the Salt Sea)\add* where the Yordan¦107933 \add river\add* flows into¦107934 it. That¦107935 was¦107936 the southern boundary
\v 20 and¦107939 the¦107939 Yordan¦107939 borders¦107940 it¦107942 on the¦107943 east¦107945. Those were¦107947 the¦107947 borders of¦107947 Benyamin's¦107949 descendants¦107948' inheritance¦107947 according to their¦107952 clans¦107952.
\rem /s1 The Towns Given to Benjamin
\p
\v 21 The¦107955 cities¦107955 allocated to¦107956 Benyamin's¦107958 descendants¦107957 and their¦107959 clans¦107959 were: Yeriho¦107960 \add !(Jericho¦107960)\add*, Beyt¦107961-Hoglah¦107963, Emek¦107964-Keziz¦107965,
\v 22 Beyt¦107967-Aravah, Zemaraim¦107969, Beyt¦107970-El¦107972,
\v 23 Avvim¦107974, Parah¦107975, Ofrah¦107976,
\v 24 Kefar-Ammoni¦107978, Ofni, and Geba¦107982—a total of twelve cities¦107983 as well as their \add surrounding\add* villages¦107987.
\v 25 \add Also\add* Gibeon¦107989, Ramah¦107990, Beerot¦107991,
\v 26 Mizpah¦107993, Kefirah¦107994, Mozah¦107995,
\v 27 Rekem¦107997, Irpeel¦107998, Taralah¦107999,
\v 28 Zelah, Haelef, Yebus (\add ≈now called\add* Yerushalem¦108006), Gibeah¦108007, and Kiriat¦108008—\add a total of\add* fourteen cities¦108009 as well as their \add surrounding\add* villages¦108013. Those were¦108015 Benyamin's¦108018 descendants¦108016' inheritance¦108015 according to¦108019 their¦108019 clans¦108019.
\c 19
\s1 The allocation to Shimeon's descendants
\rem /s1 The Territory Assigned to Simeon; The Land Given to Simeon; The Territory of Simeon; Allotment for Simeon
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 1 The¦108024 second¦108024 draw¦108023 went¦108022 to Shimeon's¦108025 (Simeon's¦108029) descendants and the land for their¦108030 clans¦108030 was¦108031 in¦108033 the¦108033 middle¦108033 of¦108034 Yehudah's¦108037 territory.
\v 2 \add @Shimeon's¦108039\add* inheritance¦108041 \add ≈included\add*: Beer¦108042-Sheba,\f + \fr 19:2 \ft TC: Ancient manuscripts differ, with some adding Sheba (possibly a mistaken reduplication) or Shema here (but that would make the total number wrong that's given in v6).\f* Moladah¦108046,\x + \xo 19:2-8: \xt 1Ch 4:28-33.\x*
\v 3 Hazarshual, Balah¦108050, Ezem¦108051,
\v 4 Eltolad¦108053, Betul¦108054, Hormah¦108055,
\v 5 Ziklag¦108057, Beyt¦108058-Markabot. Hatsarsusah,
\v 6 Beyt¦108064-Lebaot, and¦108066 Sharuhen¦108066—thirteen cities¦108067 as well as their \add surrounding\add* villages¦108071.
\p
\v 7 \add Also\add* Ain¦108073, Rimmon¦108075, Eter¦108076, and¦108077 Asha—four¦108079 cities¦108078 as well as their \add surrounding\add* villages¦108080,
\v 8 and¦108082 all¦108082 the¦108084 \add further\add* villages¦108084 around¦108086 those¦108088 cities¦108087 as far as Baalat-Beer¦108092 (\add also called\add* Ramah¦108093 of the Negev¦108094). That¦108095 was¦108096 Shimeon's¦108100 descendants¦108098' inheritance¦108096 according to¦108101 their¦108101 clans¦108101.
\v 9 This \add took away\add* some of Yehudah's¦108105 inheritance¦108106 and gave it to Shimeons descendants¦108107 because¦108109 Yehudah's¦108115 \add initial\add* area was more than¦108117 \add ≈they¦108118 needed\add*.
\s1 The allocation to Zebulun's descendants
\rem /s1 The Land Given to Zebulun; The Territory of Zebulun; Allotment for Zebulun; The Territory Assigned to Zebulun
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 10 The¦108128 third¦108128 draw¦108127 went to Zebulun's¦108130 descendants¦108129 according to¦108131 their¦108131 clans¦108131. The¦108133 \add southern\add* border¦108133 for their¦108134 inheritance¦108134 \add ≈started\add* at Sarid¦108137
\v 11 and¦108139 went¦108139 \add west\add* to¦108142 Maralah¦108143 and¦108144 Dabbeshet¦108145 then¦108146 to¦108147 the¦108149 riverbed¦108149 facing¦108153 Yokneam¦108154.
\v 12 \add Also\add* from¦108157 Sarid¦108157 it went toward the east¦108158 beside the¦108163 border¦108163 with Kislot-Tabor and¦108166 then on to¦108167 Daberat¦108169 and¦108170 then to Yafia¦108171.
\v 13 From¦108173 there¦108173 it¦108174 extended east to¦108177 Gittah-Hefer¦108178 and Ittah-Katsin and \add north\add* to Rimmon¦108182 before turning¦108183 to Neah¦108184.
\v 14 Then¦108186 \add *it\add* passed north¦108189 of¦108189 Hannaton ending¦108192 at Yiftah-El¦108196 valley¦108193.
\v 15 \add It included the cities of\add* Kattat, Nahalal¦108199, Shimron¦108200, Idalah¦108201, and¦108202 Bethlehem—\add a total of\add* twelve cities¦108204 as well as their \add surrounding\add* villages¦108208.
\v 16 That¦108210 was¦108211 Zebulun's¦108214 descendants¦108212' inheritance¦108211 according to¦108215 their¦108215 clans¦108215, \add including\add* those¦108217 cities¦108216 as well as their \add surrounding\add* villages¦108218.
\s1 The allocation to Yissakar's descendants
\rem /s1 The Territory Assigned to Issachar; Allotment for Issachar; The Territory of Issachar; The Land Given to Issachar
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 17 The¦108224 fourth¦108224 draw¦108223 went¦108222 to Yissakar's¦108226 descendants¦108225 according to¦108227 their¦108227 clans¦108227.
\v 18 \add ≈Their¦108230 land\add* \add included the cities of\add* Yezreel¦108231, Kesulot, Shunem¦108233,
\v 19 Hafaraim, Shion¦108236, Anaharat,
\v 20 Rabbit, Kishion¦108240, Ebets,
\v 21 Remet, Eyn¦108244-Gannim¦108246, Eyn¦108247-Haddah¦108248, and¦108249 Beyt¦108249-Pazzets.
\v 22 The¦108253 border¦108253 \add of their allotment\add* met with Tabor¦108254, Shahazumah, and¦108257 Beyt¦108257-Shemesh¦108258, coming out \add in the east\add* at the Yordan¦108262—\add a total of\add* sixteen cities¦108263 as well as their \add surrounding\add* villages¦108267.
\v 23 That¦108269 was¦108270 Yissakar's¦108274 descendants¦108272' inheritance¦108270 according to¦108275 their¦108275 clans¦108275, \add including\add* those cities¦108276 as well as their \add surrounding\add* villages¦108277.
\s1 The allocation to Asher's descendants
\rem /s1 The Territory of Asher; Allotment for Asher; The Land Given to Asher; The Territory Assigned to Asher
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 24 The¦108282 fifth¦108282 draw¦108281 went¦108280 to Asher's¦108286 descendants¦108284 according to¦108287 their¦108287 clans¦108287.
\v 25 \add ≈Their¦108290 land\add* \add included the cities of\add* Helkat, Hali¦108292, Beten¦108293, Akshaf¦108294,
\v 26 Allammelek, Amad¦108297, and¦108298 Mishal¦108298. Their \add western\add* \add @border¦108299\add* started at \add Mt.\add* Karmel¦108300 and¦108302 Shihorlibnat
\v 27 and¦108305 turned¦108305 back¦108305 to the east to Beyt¦108308-Dagon¦108309 and¦108310 the border with Zebulun¦108311 and¦108312 the¦108312 Yiftah-El¦108313 valley¦108315 to the north¦108316. Then it¦108320 went¦108320 to¦108316 Beyt¦108317-Emek¦108318 and¦108319 Neiel¦108319 and¦108320 north to Kabul,
\v 28 Abdon, Rehob¦108327, Hammon¦108328 and¦108329 Kanah¦108329, as far as Greater¦108332 Sidon¦108331.
\v 29 The border then¦108334 turned¦108334 back¦108334 to Ramah¦108336 and¦108337 to¦108337 the¦108339 \add ≈fortified¦108340\add* city¦108339 of¦108339 Tsor¦108342 \add (commonly known as Tyre)\add* and¦108343 turns¦108343 \add ≈west\add* to Hosah¦108345 coming out at the \add @Mediterranean\add* near Akzib¦108351.
\v 30 \add It also included\add* Ummah, Afek¦108354, and¦108355 Rehob¦108355—\add a total of\add* twenty-two cities¦108356 as well as their \add surrounding\add* villages¦108359.
\v 31 That¦108361 was¦108362 Asher's¦108366 descendants¦108364' inheritance¦108362 according to¦108367 their¦108367 clans¦108367, \add including\add* those¦108369 cities¦108368 as well as their \add surrounding\add* villages¦108370.
\s1 The allocation to Naftali's descendants
\rem /s1 Allotment for Naphtali; The Territory Assigned to Naphtali; The Territory of Naphtali; The Land Given to Naphtali
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 32 The¦108377 sixth¦108377 draw¦108376 went¦108375 to Naftali's¦108379 descendants according to¦108380 their¦108380 clans¦108380.
\v 33 Their¦108383 border¦108383 started in Helef (where there was¦108382 an oak tree¦108385 at Zaanannim¦108386) then¦108387 Adami¦108387-Nekeb¦108388 and Yabneel and on to¦108390 Lakkum¦108392 before exiting at the¦108395 Yordan¦108395.
