\v 47 Dan's border¦108507 went¦108506 out¦108506 from¦108512 them¦108512.\f + \fr 19:47 \ft Translations vary widely here because we're not sure what is meant by the literal rendering that we've kept here.\f* Then¦108513 Dan's¦108516 descendants battled against Leshem¦108520 and¦108521 captured¦108521 it¦108522 and¦108524 \add ≈slaughtered their inhabitants\add*. \add ≈So¦108529\add* they¦108529 took¦108529 it¦108530 over and¦108531 settled in¦108532 Leshem \add ≈but¦108533\add* they¦108533 renamed it to ‘Dan’ after their¦108538 ancestor¦108538.\x + \xo 19:47: \xt Jdg 18:27-29.\x*
\v 48 That¦108540 was¦108541 Dan's¦108545 descendants¦108543' inheritance¦108541 according to¦108546 their¦108546 clans¦108546, \add including\add* those¦108548 cities¦108547 as well as their \add surrounding\add* villages¦108549.
