\p
\v 50 \add ≈Following Yahweh's¦108573 instructions to¦108575 give Yehoshua whatever\add* city¦108578 he¦108580 asked¦108580 for¦108580, he was given Timnat-Serah¦108585 in¦108586 the¦108586 hill¦108586 country¦108586 of¦108586 Efrayim¦108587 and¦108588 he¦108588 built¦108588 \add up\add* that¦108579 city¦108591 and¦108592 lived¦108592 in¦108593 it¦108593.
\p
\v 51 Those¦108595 were¦108596 the¦108596 allotments that¦108597 Eleazar¦108599 the¦108600 priest¦108600 and¦108602 Yehoshua¦108602 (Nun's¦108605 son¦108603) gave¦108598 to the¦108606 \add ≈leaders\add* of¦108606 the¦108607 Israeli¦108611 tribes¦108608 as \add &their¦108609\add* inheritances¦108596. It was done by¦108613 throwing dice there in¦108615 Shiloh¦108615 in¦108616 front¦108616 of¦108616 Yahweh¦108617 at the¦108618 opening¦108618 of¦108618 the¦108619 \add sacred\add* tent¦108619, and¦108621 so the¦108625 land¦108625 division was completed¦108621.
\c 20
\s1 The refuge cities
\rem /s1 Cities of Refuge; Cities of refuge; The Cities of Refuge
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 1 Then¦108628 Yahweh¦108629 told¦108628 Yehoshua¦108632,
\v 2 “Tell¦108635 the¦108638 Israelis¦108639 to select some cities¦108645 that¦108647 people¦108638 can flee to¦108640 in order to¦108642 be safe,\x + \xo 20:2: \xt Num 35:9-34; Deu 4:41-43; 19:1-13.\x* just as I¦108649 instructed you¦108650 through¦108651 Mosheh¦108653,
\v 3 so that¦108658 if \add ≈someone accidentally¦108661 kills someone else\add*, they¦108665 can escape there and¦108665 be¦108665 safe \add ≈from¦108668 the dead person's¦108660 family\add*.
\v 4 When¦108671 \add @that¦108671 person¦108671\add* flees¦108671 to¦108672 one¦108674 of¦108676 these¦108677 cities¦108676, \add they must\add* stand¦108678 at the city gate¦108680 and¦108682 tell¦108682 the¦108684 elders¦108684 there what happened. Then¦108692 they¦108692 should bring \add @the¦108693 person¦108693\add* into¦108694 the¦108694 city¦108694 and¦108696 give¦108696 \add ≈them a¦108699 place¦108699 there to live¦108700 in\add*.
\v 5 \add ≈Now\add* if a relative of the¦108705 deceased comes to avenge¦108705 the¦108706 death, \add @the¦108710 city¦108710 elders¦108710\add* won't hand¦108710 over the¦108713 killer¦108713 because¦108715 \add ≈the death was accidental and¦108723 didn't¦108723 happen because of hate¦108725 or premeditation\add*.
\v 6 \add ≈So then that person\add* must¦108731 stay¦108731 in¦108733 the city until¦108735 they're brought before \add ≈the¦108738 panel of¦108738 judges¦108740\add*. \add If they decide that the death wasn't deliberate,\add* the¦108739 person must remain in that city until¦108741 the¦108743 death¦108743 of¦108743 the¦108744 high priest¦108744, then¦108750 they can \add freely\add* return¦108752 to¦108755 their own city and¦108758 own¦108760 home¦108760.”
\p
\v 7 \add ≈So¦108769\add* \add @the¦108769 Israelis¦108769\add* chose Kedesh¦108772 (in¦108773 the Galilee¦108773 region in¦108774 the¦108774 hill¦108774 country¦108774 of¦108774 Naftali¦108775) and¦108776 Shekem¦108778 (in¦108779 the¦108779 hill¦108779 country¦108779 of¦108779 Efrayim¦108780) and¦108781 Kiriat¦108783-Arba¦108784 (\add ≈now called\add* Hebron¦108786, in¦108787 the¦108787 hill¦108787 country¦108787 of¦108787 Yehudah¦108788).
\v 8 On the¦108790 other¦108790 side¦108790 of¦108791 the¦108791 Yordan¦108791 \add river\add*, they¦108794 chose Betser¦108797 (in¦108798 the wilderness¦108798 on the plateau¦108799 from¦108800 the¦108800 tribe¦108800 of¦108800 Reuben¦108801), Ramot¦108804 (in¦108805 the Gilead¦108805 from¦108806 the¦108806 tribe¦108806 of¦108806 Gad¦108808), and¦108809 Golan¦108811 (in¦108813 the Bashan¦108813 from¦108814 the¦108814 tribe¦108814 of¦108814 Menashsheh¦108815).
\v 9 Those¦108817 were¦108818 the¦108819 \add ≈appointed¦108820\add* cities¦108819 for \add ≈both Israelis¦108824 and¦108825 foreigners¦108825 living¦108826 among¦108827\add* them¦108827, so that anyone¦108832 who¦108832 \add ≈accidentally¦108835\add* killed someone¦108832 could flee¦108828 there and¦108836 \add ≈be safe from being avenged¦108839 by¦108838 the deceased's relatives\add* until¦108841 \add ≈they could receive a proper trial\add*.
\c 21
