\p
\v 1 Then¦108848 the \add ≈leaders\add* of the Levites¦108851 went to¦108852 Eleazar¦108854 the¦108855 priest¦108855 and¦108856 to¦108856 Yehoshua¦108858 (Nun's¦108861 son¦108859) and¦108862 to¦108862 the \add ≈Israeli¦108868 elders\add*
\v 2 at Shiloh¦108872 (in¦108873 the Canaan¦108874 region¦108873) and told¦108875 them, “Yahweh¦108876 said¦108875 \add ≈through¦108878\add* Mosheh¦108880 \add ≈that we should be given¦108881 cities¦108884 to¦108885 live¦108885 in¦108885, along with their¦108886 surrounding fields\add* for¦108887 our¦108887 livestock¦108887.”\x + \xo 21:2: \xt Num 35:1-8.\x*
\v 3 \add ≈So¦108889 the¦108890 Israeli¦108892\add* \add leaders\add* gave¦108889 these¦108902 cities¦108901 and the fields around them to¦108893 the Levites¦108893 for their¦108894 inheritance¦108894 \add ≈as Yahweh¦108898 had instructed\add*:
\p
\v 4 The¦108908 first draw¦108908 went¦108907 to those of¦108909 the¦108909 Kohat clans¦108909 \add who were\add* descendants¦108912 of¦108912 Aharon¦108913 the¦108914 priest¦108914 (from the¦108917 Levites¦108917). They were allocated thirteen cities¦108925 in the¦108918 regions occupied by Yehudah¦108919, Shimeon, and Benyamin¦108923.
\v 5 The¦108930 remaining¦108932 Kohat¦108931 \add ≈clans¦108933\add* were \add allocated\add* ten¦108945 cities¦108944 in the¦108934 regions occupied by Efrayim¦108936, Dan¦108939, and¦108940 the Menashsheh¦108942 half-tribe.
\p
\v 6 The¦108948 Gereshon¦108949 \add ≈clans¦108950\add* were \add allocated\add* thirteen cities¦108964 in the¦108951 regions occupied by Yissakar¦108953, Asher¦108956, Naftali¦108958, and¦108959 by the Menashsheh¦108961 half-tribe in¦108962 the Bashan¦108962 \add region\add*.
\p
\v 7 The¦108969 Merari¦108970 clans¦108971 were \add allocated\add* twelve cities¦108979 in the¦108972 regions occupied by Reuben¦108973, Gad¦108976, and¦108977 Zebulun¦108978.
\p
\v 8 \add ≈So¦108983 the¦108984 Israeli¦108986 leaders\add* gave¦108983 those¦108991 cities¦108990 and¦108992 their¦108994 surrounding fields to the Levites¦108987, just¦108995 as¦108995 Yahweh¦108997 had¦108996 instructed¦108996 \add ≈through¦108998\add* Mosheh¦109000.
\p
\v 9 ⇔These¦109013 are the \add #names¦109018\add* of the¦109012 cities¦109012 \add ≈allocated by the Israeli leaders (from the regions occupied by\add* Yehudah¦109007 and¦109008 Shimeon¦109010)
\v 10 that were¦109020 given to¦109021 the Levite¦109026 Kohat clans¦109023 since¦109027 \add ≈they were selected first¦109031 in the¦109030 draw¦109030\add*:
\v 11 Kiriat¦109037-Arba¦109038 and¦109045 the surrounding¦109048 fields (\add ≈now called\add* Hebron¦109042—Arba was the¦109039 father¦109039 of¦109039 Anak¦109040) in¦109043 Yehudah's¦109044 hill¦109043 country¦109043
\v 12 (although the¦109052 surrounding countryside¦109052 and¦109054 villages¦109056 had already been given¦109057 to¦109058 Yefunneh's¦109061 son¦109059 Caleb¦109058).
\v 13 \add ≈So¦109065\add* Hebron¦109077 was given¦109069 to¦109065 the¦109065 descendants¦109065 of¦109065 Aharon¦109067 the¦109068 priest¦109068 and assigned as a refuge¦109073 city¦109072 (for anyone who \add accidentally\add* kills¦109074 someone) along with the surrounding fields, along with Libnah¦109083,
\v 14 Yattir¦109090, Eshtemoa¦109096,
\v 15 Holon¦109103, Debir¦109109,
\v 16 Ain¦109116, Yuttah, and Beyt¦109128-Shemesh¦109129, all with their surrounding fields—\add a total of\add* nine¦109134 cities¦109133 from¦109135 within Yehudah and Shimeon's \add territories\add*.
\v 17 From¦109141 Benyamin's¦109142 \add territories\add*, \add the Israeli leaders\add* \add ≈assigned\add* Gibeon¦109145, Geba¦109151,
\v 18 Anatot¦109158, and Almon¦109164—four¦109169 cities¦109168 and their surrounding fields.
\v 19 \add Thus\add* the¦109174 descendants¦109174 of¦109174 Aharon¦109176 the¦109177 priests¦109177 \add received\add* thirteen cities¦109181 with their¦109182 surrounding fields.
\p
\v 20 The \add other\add* Levite¦109189 Kohat¦109192 clans¦109185 were¦109193 allocated cities¦109194 from¦109196 \add ≈within Efrayim's¦109197 territory\add*:
