\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 43 \add ≈Thus\add* Yahweh¦109590 gave¦109589 \add ≈the Israelis¦109591\add* all¦109594 the¦109596 land¦109596 that¦109597 he'd¦109598 promised¦109598 their¦109600 ancestors¦109600 would be given and¦109601 \add so the people\add* \add ≈moved into those regions\add* and¦109602 lived¦109602 there.
\v 44 Yahweh¦109606 gave¦109605 them¦109607 \add ≈peace\add* as he'd¦109612 promised¦109612 their ancestors¦109613—none of¦109613 their¦109613 enemies could stand¦109616 against them \add ≈because Yahweh¦109627 helped them defeat any enemies\add*.
\v 45 \add ≈Yahweh¦109640 kept every¦109634 promise that¦109637 he'd¦109639 made to¦109641 the¦109643 Israelis¦109644—it¦109646 all¦109634 happened just like he'd said¦109639\add*.
\c 22
\s1 The eastern tribes return home
\rem /s1 The Eastern Tribes Return to Their Territory; Eastern Tribes Return Home; Joshua Sends the Eastern Tribes Home; The Eastern Tribes Return Home
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 1 Then¦109649 Yehoshua¦109651 \add ≈summoned¦109650\add* the tribes¦109655 of¦109655 Reuben and Gad, and the Menashsheh¦109656 half-tribe
\v 2 and¦109658 told¦109658 them¦109659, “You yourselves have¦109661 obeyed¦109671 everything that¦109665 Yahweh's¦109670 servant¦109669 Mosheh¦109668 instructed¦109666 you¦109671 to do. In addition, you've all¦109673 followed everything that¦109674 I¦109676 told¦109676 you¦109677.\x + \xo 22:2: \xt Num 32:20-32; Josh 1:12-15.\x*
\v 3 You've¦109681 all \add ^supported\add* your¦109684 \add ≈fellow tribes\add* all¦109687 this¦109690 time and¦109691 fulfilled what your¦109697 god¦109697 Yahweh¦109696 \add ≈requested of¦109697 you all\add*,
\v 4 and¦109699 now¦109699 \add *he¦109701\add* has¦109700 enabled \add ≈these other tribes\add* to rest¦109700 \add from battle\add* just¦109704 like¦109704 he¦109705 told¦109705 them¦109706 he would. \add ≈So¦109707\add* now¦109707, you all may go¦109709 back to your homes¦109711 that¦109716 Yahweh's servant¦109721 Mosheh¦109720 gave¦109718 you¦109719 on¦109723 the¦109723 \add ≈other¦109723\add* side¦109723 of¦109723 the¦109724 river.
\v 5 Only¦109726 do take¦109728 care¦109728 to \add continue to\add* obey the¦109733 instructions¦109733 and¦109734 the¦109736 law¦109736 that¦109737 Yahweh's servant¦109741 Mosheh¦109740 gave you¦109739: to¦109744 love¦109744 your¦109748 god¦109748 Yahweh¦109747, to¦109749 \add ≈follow¦109749 him and his instructions\add*, to \add ≈stay close to him¦109757\add*, and¦109758 to¦109758 serve¦109758 him¦109758 with all¦109759 your¦109761 \add #hearts¦109761\add* and¦109762 your¦109764 \add inner\add* selves.”
\v 6 Then¦109766 Yehoshua¦109767 blessed¦109766 them¦109766 and¦109768 sent¦109768 them¦109768 on their way to return¦109769 to¦109770 their¦109772 \add ≈homes¦109772\add*.
\v 7 (Mosheh¦109780 had¦109779 given¦109779 the Bashan¦109781 to¦109782 the half¦109782 of¦109782 the Menashsheh¦109778 half-tribe, and Yehoshua¦109784 had¦109783 given¦109783 \add land\add* on¦109788 the¦109788 \add ≈western¦109792\add* side¦109788 of¦109788 the¦109791 Yordan¦109791 to¦109797 the other¦109788 half.) \add When\add* he'd¦109800 blessed¦109800 them¦109800
\v 8 he'd¦109802 said¦109802, “Go back to your \add ≈homes¦109810\add* with¦109805 many¦109820 riches¦109805: plenty of livestock¦109811, and with¦109815 silver¦109815, gold¦109816, bronze¦109817, and¦109818 iron¦109818, and¦109819 with¦109819 lots of clothing¦109819. Share the¦109823 plunder¦109823 from your¦109825 enemies¦109825 with¦109826 \add ≈those who remained behind\add*.”
\v 9 \add ≈So\add* \add ≈the¦109836 warriors from the¦109841 tribes¦109841 of¦109833\add* Reuven¦109835, Gad¦109838, and¦109839 the Menashsheh¦109842 half-tribe left the¦109844 \add ≈others\add* there at Shiloh¦109846 in¦109848 the Canaan¦109850 region, and went¦109851 back to¦109852 their¦109859 own¦109859 land¦109854 in Gilead¦109855 \add across the river\add* which¦109860 they¦109861 had¦109861 taken for themselves with the¦109866 agreement of¦109866 Yahweh¦109867 given through¦109868 Mosheh¦109870.
\s1 The altar by the Yordan
\rem /s1 A Memorial Altar East of the Jordan; The Altar by the Jordan; The Eastern Tribes Build a Memorial
\s4 Promised land
\p
\v 10 \add ≈The¦109876 warriors from the¦109881 tribes¦109888 of\add* Reuven¦109883, Gad¦109886, and¦109887 the Menashsheh¦109889 half-tribe arrived¦109872 at¦109892 the¦109894 Yordan¦109894 \add river\add* (\add still\add* on the Canaan¦109879 side) and¦109880 they¦109880 built¦109880 a very large¦109896 and noticeable altar there¦109890 \add before crossing over to go home\add*.
\v 11 \add When\add* the¦109900 \add other\add* \add ≈Israelis¦109900\add* heard¦109899 \add about it\add*, they said¦109903, “Look, the¦109909 men \add ≈from the¦109913 tribes¦109913 of¦109906\add* Reuven¦109908, Gad¦109911, and¦109912 the Menashsheh¦109914 half-tribe have¦109905 built¦109905 the¦109917 altar¦109917 at the \add ≈entrance to this\add* Canaan¦109922 region¦109921 down at the¦109926 Yordan¦109926 on \add *our\add* side¦109929.”
\p
\v 12 \add ≈Hearing¦109933 that, those from the¦109939 western side of¦109939 the¦109940 Yordan assembled¦109936 at Shiloh¦109943 to¦109944 go¦109944 to battle¦109946 with the two and a half tribes on¦109945 the eastern side\add*.
\v 13 ⇔\add Meanwhile\add*, they¦109949 sent¦109949 the¦109979 priest¦109979 Finehas¦109975 (Eleazar's¦109978 son¦109976) \add across\add* into the Gilead¦109972 region¦109971 \add to talk\add* with \add the leaders from\add* the tribes¦109966 of Reuben¦109957, Gad¦109962, and¦109963 the¦109965 Menashsheh¦109968 half-tribe.
\v 14 \add @Finehas\add* took ten¦109981 leaders¦109982 with¦109983 him¦109983—important leaders from each of the Israeli¦110000 tribes¦109991 \add from the western side\add*.
\v 15 ⇔They¦110002 \add crossed over\add* to the Gilead¦110022 region¦110021 to talk¦110023 to \add the leaders from\add* the tribes¦110016 of Reuben¦110007, Gad¦110012, and¦110013 the¦110015 Menashsheh¦110018 half-tribe. They said¦110025,
